# .cursorrules — Knowledge Hub Agent Behavior

> This file defines permanent rules for every Cursor agent working on this codebase.
> It is the "System Prompt" for the knowledge-hub project.
> Lil Claw / Goop updates this file when architecture decisions change.
> Read this file at the start of every session.

---

## Project Context

**What this is:** A finance knowledge hub — transforming dense wiki content (corporate actions, index methodology, vendor comparisons) into a beautiful, interactive web interface.

**Stack:** React 19 + Next.js (App Router) + Tailwind CSS v4 + shadcn/ui + Framer Motion + Lucide React + TypeScript (strict)

**Design philosophy:** "Modern, Clean, Smooth, Minimalist" — glassmorphism, bento box layouts, high-contrast typography, dark mode default.

**Live URL:** https://zeimhahnu.github.io/knowledge-hub/

---

## Communication Protocol

### The Three Channels
- **GitHub** = Source of truth for code and specs
- **Obsidian** = Executive dashboard (Alex's view of knowledge)
- **Telegram** = Real-time chat with Lil Claw / Goop

### Who Does What

| Agent | Role | Responsibility |
|-------|------|----------------|
| **Lil Claw** | Orchestrator | Market intel, research, strategic oversight |
| **Goop** | Product Owner | Specs, design system, frontend decisions |
| **Cursor** | Developer | Code implementation, UI perfection |
| **Alex** | Executive / QA | Approves specs, reviews visually |

### The Handoff Protocol

```
Alex → Telegram → Lil Claw: "I want [feature]"
         ↓
Lil Claw → Telegram → Goop: "New feature request — write spec"
         ↓
Goop → SPECS/inbox/ → [writes feature-idea.md]
         ↓
Cursor → reads SPECS/inbox/ → drafts PRD → SPECS/outbox/
         ↓
Lil Claw → reads PRD → Telegram → Alex: "Here's the PRD, approve?"
         ↓
Alex → "approved" → Goop moves to SPECS/approved/
         ↓
Cursor → implements → git push → GitHub Pages deploys
         ↓
Goop → monitors GitHub → Telegram → Alex: "Deployed! [URL]"
```

---

## Design Rules (Never Break These)

### Colors
- Primary: `#007bff` (CTAs, links)
- Secondary: `#6c757d` (muted text)
- Background: `#f8f9fa` (light) / `#0f1117` (dark)
- Border: `#e5e7eb`
- Always use Tailwind token classes: `bg-primary`, `text-foreground`, `border-border`

### Icons
- **Lucide React ONLY** — never emoji, never raw SVG unless it's a custom logo
- Sizes: `h-4 w-4` (inline), `h-5 w-5` (buttons), `h-8 w-8` (feature icons)

### Components
- **shadcn/ui primitives first** — button, card, badge, dialog, tabs, table, accordion
- One component per file: `CorporateActionCard.tsx`
- Props interface always at top: `interface Props { ... }`

### Styling
- Tailwind ONLY — no inline styles, no CSS modules
- Standard spacing: `p-2` `p-4` `p-6` `gap-4` `gap-6`
- Never arbitrary values: `top-[17px]` → use Tailwind scale

### Animations
- **Framer Motion** — fade, stagger, spring presets in design-system.md
- No CSS transitions for React components

### Accessibility
- WCAG 2.1 AA minimum
- Keyboard navigation on all interactive elements
- ARIA labels on icon-only buttons
- Color contrast 4.5:1 minimum

---

## File Conventions

| Pattern | Example |
|---------|---------|
| Components | `PascalCase.tsx` — `CorporateActionCard.tsx` |
| Hooks | `camelCase.ts` — `useAnimationState.ts` |
| Utilities | `camelCase.ts` — `formatCurrency.ts` |
| Specs | `kebab-case.md` — `dark-mode-toggle.md` |

---

## Before Every Commit

Run these checks:
```bash
npm run lint
npx tsc --noEmit
```

---

## Specs Workflow

### Folder Structure
```
SPECS/
  inbox/        ← Feature ideas from Lil Claw / Goop
  outbox/       ← Draft PRDs from Cursor
  approved/     ← Alex-approved specs (ready to build)
  archive/      ← Completed specs
```

### Spec File Template
```markdown
# Feature: [Name]

## Context
Why does this feature exist? What problem does it solve?

## Design Direction
How should it look? (参考: design-system.md)

## Technical Notes
Any constraints, dependencies, or technical considerations?

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] Criteria 1
- [ ] Criteria 2
```

---

## Git Protocol

- Commit messages: `feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, `docs:`, `style:`
- One logical unit per commit (one component, one fix)
- Branch: `main` only — no feature branches
- After every successful commit: GitHub Pages auto-deploys

